@Service
public class PermitService {
    apply(ApplyPermitRequest req):
        now = clock.instant()
        // idempotency pre-check
        existing = repo.findByRequestId(req.requestId())
        if present: if paramsMatch → return existing; else throw IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT (and log rejection? 异参409 — spec says rejections recorded for 拒绝依据; I'll record it too)
        tx:
            state = repo.lockBridgeState()
            re-check findByRequestId (inside tx) — same handling
            validate overweight: req.totalMassKg > state.maxTotalMassKg → record rejection + throw OVERWEIGHT
            validate time regression: plannedEntryAt.isBefore(now) → rejection + TIME_REGRESSION
            window = [planned, planned+crossingMinutes)
            occupying = repo.findOccupying()
            for each: occupation interval; if overlaps → rejection + WINDOW_OVERLAP
            insert permit; catch DuplicateKeyException → re-read, paramsMatch ? return : conflict
```

Note: rejection insert + throw → transaction rollback would roll back the rejection record too! Careful: if apply() is @Transactional and we insert rejection then throw, both roll back. Options: don't make the whole apply transactional for rejection path; or record rejection in a separate transaction (REQUIRES_NEW); or validate first, then in a transactional method do lock+overlap+insert. 

Design: split into two methods:
- `apply(req)` — non-transactional facade: idempotency pre-check, cheap validations (overweight, time regression) outside tx? But overweight check needs config from DB (non-locking read ok). Then call transactional `issuePermit(req, now)` that locks, re-checks idempotency, re-validates, checks overlap, inserts. If issuePermit throws PermitConflictException, facade records rejection (outside the rolled-back tx, in a new tx via self-injection or repository call in no-tx context — JdbcTemplate autocommit works fine) and rethrows.

But there's a subtlety: rejection recorded after rollback — good. But concurrent failures could double-record rejections — acceptable (rejection log allows duplicates).

Also validation inside the lock: re-validate overweight/time inside tx? Config can't change (seeded), time regression check with same `now`. To keep single source of truth, do all validation inside the transactional method, and facade catches PermitConflictException from issue and records rejection. But idempotency conflict (different params) — is that a "拒绝" to record? "查询展示…拒绝依据" mainly for 超重/倒退/重叠. I'll record all rejection-ish conflicts except... keep it simple: record OVERWEIGHT, TIME_REGRESSION, WINDOW_OVERLAP; for IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT also record (reason_code exists in schema comment). Fine.

