import java.util.List;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.BeforeEach;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.boot.test.context.SpringBootTest;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Import;
import org.springframework.jdbc.core.JdbcTemplate;

import com.example.starter.bridge.dto.ApplyPermitRequest;
import com.example.starter.bridge.dto.TimelineResponse;

@SpringBootTest
@Import(TestClockConfiguration.class)
class PermitServiceIntegrationTest {

    @Autowired PermitService permitService;
    @Autowired MutableClock clock;
    @Autowired JdbcTemplate jdbcTemplate;

    @BeforeEach
    void cleanUp() {
        jdbcTemplate.update("DELETE FROM bridge_permit");
        jdbcTemplate.update("DELETE FROM bridge_rejection");
        clock.set(TestClockConfiguration.BASE_TIME);
    }

    private ApplyPermitRequest request(String requestId, String plate, int massKg, String plannedAt) {
        return new ApplyPermitRequest(requestId, plate, massKg, Instant.parse(plannedAt));
    }
    ...
}
```

Tests:
1. mainFlow: apply 34000 at 09:00 → APPROVED, window [09:00,09:10). clock 09:02 → confirmEntry → ENTERED actualEntryAt 09:02. clock 09:12 → confirmExit → EXITED actualExitAt 09:12. timeline entries size 1, occupiedFrom 09:02, occupiedTo 09:12.
2. overweightRejectedAndKeyReusable: apply 36000 → PermitConflictException code OVERWEIGHT; findByRequestId empty; rejection row count 1 with code OVERWEIGHT; retry same requestId with 34000 → success.
3. timeRegressionRejected: clock at 09:00, planned 08:59 → TIME_REGRESSION.
4. windowOverlapRejected: apply A 09:00; apply B 09:05 → WINDOW_OVERLAP; apply C 09:10 (adjacent, no overlap) → success.
5. entryOnlyWithinWindow: apply 09:00; clock 08:59 entry → OUTSIDE_WINDOW; clock 09:10 entry → OUTSIDE_WINDOW; clock 09:05 entry → ok.
6. enteredOccupiesUntilExit: apply 09:00, clock 09:05 entry; clock 09:15 apply B at 09:15 → WINDOW_OVERLAP; clock 09:20 exit; apply B at 09:20 → success.
7. cancelReleasesWindow: apply A 09:00; cancel A → CANCELLED; apply B 09:00 → success.
8. enteredPermitNotCancellable: apply, enter, cancel → NOT_CANCELLABLE.
9. idempotentApplyReplay: apply; apply same params same requestId → same id; different params → IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT; still one permit row.
10. entryExitReplayDoesNotOverwrite: apply 09:00, clock 09:02 entry "op-e1"; clock 09:03 entry "op-e1" replay → actualEntryAt still 09:02; entry "op-e2" → IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT. clock 09:12 exit "op-x1"; clock 09:13 exit "op-x1" → actualExitAt 09:12; exit "op-x2" → conflict.
11. exitBeforeEntryRejected: apply, enter at 09:05, clock 09:04 exit → TIME_REGRESSION. Wait clock must go backwards — set clock 09:04 after entering at 09:05. exit → TIME_REGRESSION. Good.
12. cancelReplay: cancel twice same key → ok; different key → conflict.
13. exitWithoutEntry → INVALID_STATE.

That's a lot; split into two files or accept ~250 lines. Instruction: single write ~200 lines max, long files in segments. I'll write the file in two appends.

Then PermitConcurrencyTest:
1. concurrentApplySameWindow: two threads apply different requestIds, same window 09:00 (clock fixed at 08:00 say; planned 09:00 in future). Exactly one success, one PermitConflictException WINDOW_OVERLAP; one permit row.
2. concurrentApplySameRequestId: two threads same requestId same params → both succeed, same permit id, one row.
3. entryVsCancelRace: permit approved (window starts 09:00, clock set 09:05 so entry is within window). Two threads: confirmEntry("op-e") and cancel("op-c"). Exactly one succeeds; final status is ENTERED or CANCELLED; the loser gets PermitConflictException. Verify final DB state consistent.

Use ExecutorService, CountDownLatch start gate, futures with get(15, SECONDS).

Concurrency note: H2 with Hikari pool size 8 — fine.

Potential deadlock: two concurrent apply both lock bridge_state row FOR UPDATE — serialized, fine.

PermitApiTest with MockMvc: synthetic scenario. JSON body with Instant strings "2026-10-04T09:00:00Z". Jackson handles Instant via jsr310 (in spring-boot-starter-web). 

Scenario:
- clock 08:50. POST /api/bridge/permits {req-a, CAR-34T, 34000, 09:00} → 201, status APPROVED, windowEnd 09:10.
- POST {req-b, CAR-33T, 33000, 09:05} → 409 code WINDOW_OVERLAP.
- clock 09:03. POST /permits/{id}/entry {op-e1} → 200 ENTERED.
- POST {req-b2, CAR-33T, 33000, 09:11} → 409 WINDOW_OVERLAP (still on bridge).
- clock 09:12. POST exit {op-x1} → EXITED.
- POST {req-b3, CAR-33T, 33000, 09:12} → 201.
- GET /timeline → maxTotalMassKg 35000, crossingMinutes 10, entries 2, rejections contains req-b and req-b2 with WINDOW_OVERLAP.
- GET /permits/9999 → 404.
- POST invalid (missing requestId) → 400.

Also idempotent replay via API: POST same req-a same body → 200 same id; POST req-a different mass → 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT.

TimeWindowsTest: pure unit — overlaps cases including null ends.

Write integration test part 1 now.

